<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dmitry of Uglich</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1582–1591</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Tsarevich Dmitry, Dmitry Ivanovich</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dmitry of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uglich">Uglich</a> was the youngest son of Ivan the Terrible. After his father's death he lived with his mother at Uglich, where in 1591 he died of a knife wound to the throat. An official inquiry called it an accident during an epileptic fit, but many blamed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boris-godunov">Boris Godunov</a>. Several pretenders later claimed his name, and he was canonised in 1606.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dmitry-of-uglich.jpg" alt="Dmitry of Uglich" width="320" height="370" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mikhail Nesterov · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1899._Tzarevich_Dmitry_by_M._Nesterov.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
